    ('request_latency', map('lb','a'), map(), toDateTime64('2026-01-01 00:00:00', 9), 8, 16.0, [1,3,2,2], [1.0,2.0,4.0]),
    ('request_latency', map('lb','b'), map(), toDateTime64('2025-12-31 23:59:00', 9), 5, 7.0,  [3,1,0,1], [1.0,2.0,4.0]),
    ('request_latency', map('lb','b'), map(), toDateTime64('2026-01-01 00:00:00', 9), 9, 20.0, [1,1,5,2], [1.0,2.0,3.0]);
-- expected_rows --
[]
-- description --
The range form of histogram_quantile_classic_min_over_time_by_le: a one-minute
step grid whose later windows drop the older samples of each series, so the
quantile moves across the steps. The range lowering reduces each (series,
step) window with the same per-rung fold as the instant one.
